                <head>353. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>Prime Minister Pipinelis resigned on September 26 following protests by the
                    Center Union that his links with ERE and the repeated election law violations
                    during the 1961 campaign necessitated a neutral figure at the head of the Greek
                    Government during national elections. King Paul asked the President of the
                    Supreme Court, Stylianos Mavromichalies, to form a government to oversee
                    elections. Mavromichalies presented his government to Parliament on September 28
                    and announced that the King would call new elections for November 3.</p>
            </div>
